SWEET USB live-log port (patch 0152): boot-arg sweetusblogport=N (1..65535) sends the UDP console log (patch 0075) to 192.168.7.1:N instead of 5140.
Without the boot-arg nothing changes. No hardware access. Reason: the host firewall (NixOS networking.firewall) drops UDP 5140 when it is active (observed 2026-11-15 c4-batt5:
rx counters rose, listener got 0 bytes, firewall.service active); 64738 is already in allowedUDPPorts.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
@@ -845,7 +845,11 @@
 	bzero(&to, sizeof(to));
 	to.sin_len = sizeof(to);
 	to.sin_family = AF_INET;
-	to.sin_port = htons(5140);
+	uint32_t port = 5140;
+	if (!PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetusblogport", &port, sizeof(port)) || port == 0 || port > 65535) {
+		port = 5140;            /* boot-arg sweetusblogport=N (patch 0152): another UDP port for a host firewall that blocks 5140 */
+	}
+	to.sin_port = htons((uint16_t)port);
 	to.sin_addr.s_addr = htonl(0xc0a80701);         /* 192.168.7.1 */
 	for (;;) {
 		ud_sleep_ms(100);
